Private and shared cache stress
===============================

Part of HW_Specific: tests that stress one hardware resource, to study how
interference on it shows up in other partitions. The sizes come from
BENCH_TOOLS/arch_config.h (cache and TLB geometry of the target).

What it tests
-------------

Cache management by the OS: hits, misses and eviction when the caches are
filled.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Every 200 ms walks byte by byte over data the size of the last-level cache (L3
on x86_64, L2 on Cortex-A53), reading it (CACHE_RDONLY = 1) or writing it.
Smaller WALK_SIZE values study the private caches; CACHE_PRELOAD_L2/L3 preload
a level and evict the ones above it.

Expected output
---------------

"Cache flooded 100 times" every 100 periods (20 s).

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/CACHE_PRIVATE_SHARED/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/HW_Specific/CACHES/CACHE_PRIVATE_SHARED/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
